# [ASDF](../wg/asdf.html)

## Summary

The ASDF Working Group held an interim meeting to review updates to active working group specifications and discuss implementation experience with RFC 9880. Jungha Hong presented revisions to `draft-ietf-asdf-digital-twin` (v06) and `draft-ietf-asdf-sdf-nonaffordance` (v06). Peder Bergan introduced a new open-source implementation of SDF (ESDIEFF) and presented eight specific technical questions regarding RFC 9880 resolution, inheritance, and grammar rules. 

## Key Discussion Points

### Working Group & Document Status
* Lorenzo Corneo noted that the Area Director evaluation has commenced for the NIPC and SDF protocol mapping specifications.

### SDF Modeling for Digital Twin
* Jungha Hong presented updates for `draft-ietf-asdf-digital-twin` based on the presentation [SDF modeling for Digital Twin (v06)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-asdf-07/materials/slides-interim-2026-asdf-07-sessa-sdf-modeling-for-digital-twin-v06-00).
* Key updates in draft version 06 include:
  * Alignment of `sdfContext` and `sdfRelation` wording with the extension draft.
  * Clarification of `sdfRelation` representation beyond simple containment (using target and relation type, keeping protocol bindings at the affordance level).
  * Simplification and alignment of marine and healthcare examples.
  * Expansion of the smart building example to include heterogeneous systems (Matter, BACnet, KNX, CoAP, MQTT).
  * Refinement of the smart network scenario and expansion of cross-domain synchronization and state consistency requirements.
  * Detail added to Section 8 covering implementation procedures.
* Ari Keränen inquired about whether specific data models were assumed for the CoAP and MQTT smart building examples alongside ecosystems with defined data models (KNX, Matter, BACnet). Jungha Hong agreed to coordinate an email response from co-authors.
* Lorenzo Corneo and Jan Romann noted the synergy between the digital twin bindings and the ongoing CoAP protocol mapping effort, emphasizing the goal to publish an initial draft version of the CoAP protocol mapping.

### SDF Extension for Non-Affordance Information (`sdfContext`)
* Jungha Hong presented updates for `draft-ietf-asdf-sdf-nonaffordance` based on the presentation [Slides-draft-asdf-sdf-nonaffordance](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-asdf-07/materials/slides-interim-2026-asdf-07-sessa-slides-draft-asdf-sdf-nonaffordance-00).
* Key structural changes:
  * Runtime context message sections were removed to keep the specification focused exclusively on the static model extension. Runtime aspects will be integrated into the instance information draft framework in collaboration with Carsten Bormann.
  * `sdfType` link discussion (referencing `draft-ietf-asdf-sdftype-link`) was moved to the examples section.
  * Added Section 6 to clarify relationships with other SDF documents.
  * `sdfContext` is established as a new class keyword allowed inside `sdfObject` and `sdfThing` (not permitted at the root level).
  * Clarified the distinction between `sdfContext` (descriptive metadata; no protocol endpoints/getters/putters generated) and `sdfProperty` (interactive read/write capability).
* Peder Bergan reported that implementation planning for the non-affordance extension is underway.
* Ari Keränen suggested renaming `draft-ietf-asdf-sdf-nonaffordance` to incorporate `sdfContext` in the draft name now that terminology has converged.

### RFC 9880 Implementation Questions
* Peder Bergan presented implementation feedback based on building an open-source SDF implementation (ESDIEFF), detailed in [RFC 9880 implementation questions](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-asdf-07/materials/slides-interim-2026-asdf-07-sessa-rfc-9880-implementation-questions-00).
* The discussion covered eight specific topics:
  1. **References inside copied/inherited definitions**: Resolving `sdfRef` targets when definitions inherit from a base definition that contains references and local overrides. Carsten Bormann and Ari Keränen discussed RFC 9880 resolution behavior (merge patch principles) and suggested establishing clear terminology (e.g., differentiating copying vs `sdfRef` resolution).
  2. **Required declarations in inherited definitions**: Pointers in `sdfRequired` relocating to corresponding targets in inherited object instances.
  3. **Namespaces in inherited references**: Preserving prefix-to-namespace map bindings from the source document versus applying the importing document's namespace map upon explicit overrides.
  4. **Forms permitted by grammar**: Clarifying that `sdfRef: true` is an artifact of CDDL definitions lacking defined semantics, whereas single-name `sdfRef` strings represent sibling references within the same object context.
  5. **Array item nullability and imported qualities**: Interaction of default nullability with imported qualities via `sdfRef`.
  6. **Required markers in data-only definitions**: `sdfRequired` within standalone `sdfData` taking effect only when imported into an `sdfProperty` context.
  7. **Empty documents and definition groups**: Distinguishing between syntactic validity (empty JSON objects/groups are valid SDF syntactically) and semantic usefulness (empty structures define no usable targets).
  8. **Byte string constraints**: Interpreting byte string length constraints as counting octets rather than encoded text characters.

